            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0170" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg54"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/705.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-11-29T13:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 29, 1911—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The information requested in your November 28, 3 p.m., came from the Viceroy at
                    Mukden, and the Foreign Office regards it as reliable. The representations were
                    made to me at the same time as to the British, German and Japanese Ministers.
                    The latter denied all knowledge of the matter and promised to telegraph his
                    Government to use its good offices to remove the causes of complaint.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
